#
# Declarative structural assertions for the slice-quality-rubric slice — the
# MUST / MUST-NOT invariants of the rubric-as-data spine, run as SPARQL ASK over
# the module graph (gmeow:scopeModule) under the native Rust harness
# (crates/slicetest). Each rationale states the ONTOLOGICAL reason the invariant
# holds and names no test artifact — this slice is the exemplar of the
# provenance-honesty rule it defines.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/slice-quality-rubric/tests/> .

# --- 1. The rubric is one Profile over Slice carrying all six descriptors -----
ex:saRubricProfileShape a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:sliceQualityRubric a gmeow:Profile ;
        gmeow:profileDescriptor gmeow:axisProducer , gmeow:axisDimension ,
            gmeow:axisThreshold , gmeow:axisAdviceTemplate , gmeow:axisWeight ,
            gmeow:axisContextScope ;
        gmeow:profileOpenValue gmeow:SliceQualityDimension , gmeow:AxisContextScope .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The rubric is data, not code: a single gmeow:Profile over gmeow:Slice must enumerate exactly the six axis-descriptor properties and the three open value vocabularies, so tooling reads the axes, tiers, and scopes from the ontology rather than from a Rust fork." .

# --- 2. QualityTier is an open value vocabulary of individuals (MUST) ----------
ex:saTierIsValueVocab a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:QualityTier a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The tier ladder is a bounded lattice of grades, so gmeow:QualityTier is an open value vocabulary of individuals subclassing logic:QualityValue — a new tier is a minted individual with a fresh rank, never a subclass (Principle 9)." .

# --- 3. The five tier rungs exist with contiguous distinct ranks (MUST) --------
ex:saTierLadder a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:tierRegistered  a gmeow:QualityTier ; gmeow:tierRank 0 .
    gmeow:tierGrounded    a gmeow:QualityTier ; gmeow:tierRank 1 .
    gmeow:tierLinked      a gmeow:QualityTier ; gmeow:tierRank 2 .
    gmeow:tierExemplified a gmeow:QualityTier ; gmeow:tierRank 3 .
    gmeow:tierMaximal     a gmeow:QualityTier ; gmeow:tierRank 4 .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The lattice order is carried by gmeow:tierRank, so the five rungs must exist with contiguous distinct ranks from 0 to 4; the roll-up tier is the meet (least rank) of a slice's per-axis grades and is undefined without a total order." .

# --- 4. QualityAxis is an open value vocabulary of individuals (MUST) ----------
ex:saAxisIsValueVocab a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:QualityAxis a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ;
        rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Extensibility-by-construction requires that a new measured axis be a minted individual binding a primitive, not a code fork, so gmeow:QualityAxis is an open value vocabulary of individuals subclassing logic:QualityValue." .

# --- 5. Every axis binds a producer, a dimension, a scope, and a threshold -----
ex:saAxesFullyBound a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    gmeow:axisMaximalGrounding    gmeow:axisProducer ?p1 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d1 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s1 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t1 .
    gmeow:axisReasonerDerived     gmeow:axisProducer ?p2 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d2 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s2 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t2 .
    gmeow:axisMaximalInformation  gmeow:axisProducer ?p3 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d3 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s3 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t3 .
    gmeow:axisMaximalLinkage      gmeow:axisProducer ?p4 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d4 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s4 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t4 .
    gmeow:axisMaximalProjection   gmeow:axisProducer ?p5 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d5 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s5 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t5 .
    gmeow:axisOptimalTesting      gmeow:axisProducer ?p6 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d6 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s6 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t6 .
    gmeow:axisDocumentation       gmeow:axisProducer ?p7 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d7 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s7 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t7 .
    gmeow:axisProseQuality        gmeow:axisProducer ?p8 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d8 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s8 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t8 .
    gmeow:axisProvenanceHonesty   gmeow:axisProducer ?p9 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d9 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s9 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t9 .
    gmeow:axisTranslationCoverage gmeow:axisProducer ?p10 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d10 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s10 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t10 .
    gmeow:axisShapeMigration      gmeow:axisProducer ?p11 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d11 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s11 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t11 .
    gmeow:axisFlagshipCounterExampleDepth gmeow:axisProducer ?p12 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d12 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s12 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t12 .
    gmeow:axisGmn1Coverage        gmeow:axisProducer ?p13 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d13 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s13 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t13 .
    gmeow:axisGmnGlyphOptimality  gmeow:axisProducer ?p14 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d14 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s14 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t14 .
    gmeow:axisDocMaturity         gmeow:axisProducer ?p15 ; gmeow:axisDimension ?d15 ; gmeow:axisContextScope ?s15 ; gmeow:axisThreshold ?t15 .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Every axis must bind a measurement primitive, an emitted quality dimension, a read-scope coeffect, and at least one tier threshold, because an axis with no producer cannot be scored and an unknown producer is a hard fail rather than a silent skip." .

# --- 6. Every exemption is dated and names its producer and axis (MUST) --------
ex:saExemptionsWellFormed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    ?e a gmeow:AxisExemption ;
        gmeow:exemptsAxis ?ax ;
        gmeow:exemptionReason ?r ;
        gmeow:exemptionDate ?d ;
        gmeow:exemptionProducer ?p .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "An exemption is a dated, self-cleaning artifact, so each must name the axis it covers, a doctrine-anchored reason, the date it was minted, and the producer symbol whose landing retires it — an undated or producerless exemption would be permanent optionality." .

# --- 8b. An AxisFloorCommitment carries exactly one slice, axis, and value (MUST)
ex:saAxisFloorCommitmentWellFormed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:AxisFloorCommitment a owl:Class .
    gmeow:floorSlice a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:Slice .
    gmeow:floorAxis  a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:QualityAxis .
    gmeow:floorValue a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A per-axis floor commitment is a raise-only ratchet cell pairing one slice, one axis, and one measured-score floor, so gmeow:floorSlice, gmeow:floorAxis, and gmeow:floorValue each carry their committed ranges; their single-valued (functional) characteristic is now asserted on the logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion carrier and enforced by the DL reasoner, not in the slice module — a commitment with two slices, two axes, or two floors would make the regression bar ill-defined." .

# --- 8c. A SliceTierFloor carries exactly one slice and one tier (MUST) ---------
ex:saSliceTierFloorWellFormed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:SliceTierFloor a owl:Class .
    gmeow:floorSlice a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:Slice .
    gmeow:floorTier  a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:QualityTier .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A per-slice tier floor is a raise-only ratchet cell pairing one slice with one minimum roll-up tier, so gmeow:floorSlice and gmeow:floorTier each carry their committed ranges; their single-valued (functional) characteristic is now asserted on the logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion carrier and enforced by the DL reasoner, not in the slice module — a floor naming two slices or two tiers would make the committed rung ill-defined over the lattice order." .

# --- 8d. A ProjectionCeilingCommitment carries exactly one slice, vocabulary, and count (MUST)
ex:saProjectionCeilingCommitmentWellFormed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment a owl:Class .
    gmeow:ceilingSlice      a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:Slice .
    gmeow:ceilingVocabulary a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range gmeow:ProjectionVocabulary .
    gmeow:ceilingCount      a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A projection-ceiling commitment is a lower-only ratchet cell pairing exactly one slice, one guarded projection vocabulary, and one measured residue ceiling, so gmeow:ceilingSlice, gmeow:ceilingVocabulary, and gmeow:ceilingCount each carry their committed ranges; their single-valued (functional) characteristic is now asserted on the logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion carrier and enforced by the DL reasoner, not in the slice module — a commitment with two slices, two vocabularies, or two counts would make the monotone lower-only bar ill-defined." .

# --- 8e. A ProjectionVocabulary names its join key and its recognition strategy (MUST)
ex:saProjectionVocabularyWellFormed a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:ProjectionVocabulary a owl:Class .
    gmeow:vocabularyPrefix    a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
    gmeow:vocabularyCountKind a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A guarded projection vocabulary is looked up by exactly one short CURIE prefix and dispatches its residue-recognition strategy on exactly one closed-set count-kind literal, so gmeow:vocabularyPrefix and gmeow:vocabularyCountKind each carry their string range; their single-valued (functional) characteristic is now asserted on the logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion carrier and enforced by the DL reasoner, not in the slice module — two prefixes would break the join key a ceiling commitment resolves against, and two count-kinds would leave the shared counter's dispatch ambiguous." .

# --- 8f. No ProjectionCeilingCommitment double-binds its slice, vocabulary, or count (MUST-NOT)
ex:saProjectionCeilingNotDoubleSliced a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
ASK {
    { ?pcc a gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment ; gmeow:ceilingSlice ?s1 ; gmeow:ceilingSlice ?s2 . FILTER (?s1 != ?s2) }
    UNION
    { ?pcc a gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment ; gmeow:ceilingVocabulary ?v1 ; gmeow:ceilingVocabulary ?v2 . FILTER (?v1 != ?v2) }
    UNION
    { ?pcc a gmeow:ProjectionCeilingCommitment ; gmeow:ceilingCount ?c1 ; gmeow:ceilingCount ?c2 . FILTER (?c1 != ?c2) }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "A ceiling commitment is a single ratchet cell for one (slice, vocabulary) pair, so no individual may bind two distinct slices, two distinct vocabularies, or two distinct counts — a double-bound cell would leave the gate reading an arbitrary one of the pairings and the lower-only bar undefined for the other." .

# --- 8. The advice weight never enters the roll-up: it is not the meet (MUST-NOT)
ex:saWeightNotTierRank a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    { gmeow:axisWeight rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:tierRank }
    UNION
    { gmeow:axisWeight rdfs:range gmeow:QualityTier }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The roll-up tier is the unweighted lattice meet of the axis grades, so the advice weight must not be wired into the tier order; a weighted meet would be an ad-hoc average and would break the ratchet-is-lattice-order law." .

# --- 9. A per-axis grade carries its axis as first-class data (MUST) -----------
ex:saAssessmentAxisIsFirstClass a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:assessmentAxis a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:QualityAssessment ;
        rdfs:range gmeow:QualityAxis .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The axis a grade measured is measurement identity, not presentation, so it must be recoverable from the assessment itself: gmeow:axisDimension maps sixteen axes onto twelve dimensions, so gmeow:qualityDimension cannot recover the axis, and a minted subject IRI is a naming convention rather than an assertion." .

# --- 10. The axis is NOT recoverable via the dimension: the map is lossy (MUST-NOT)
ex:saAssessmentAxisNotAliasedToDimension a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    { gmeow:assessmentAxis rdfs:subPropertyOf gmeow:qualityDimension }
    UNION
    { gmeow:assessmentAxis owl:equivalentProperty gmeow:qualityDimension }
    UNION
    { gmeow:axisDimension a owl:InverseFunctionalProperty }
}""" ;
    gmeow:saFailWitness "tests/counter-examples/assessment-axis-aliased-to-dimension.ttl" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Several axes deliberately publish under one ISO dimension, so the axis-to-dimension map is many-to-one; declaring the axis a sub-property or equivalent of the dimension — or the dimension map injective — would assert a bijection the rubric does not have and would license recovering the axis from the dimension." .
